# Credits

assay-signals stands on a few simple things.

- [assay](https://github.com/bl888m/assay) , the six-agent desk whose --json
  output this tool reshapes. Without the desk there is nothing to reshape.
- The Python standard library , csv, json and argparse do all the work here.
  Zero third-party dependencies, on purpose.
- The favorite-longshot literature and the Kelly criterion , the ideas behind
  the numbers assay produces, credited in full in the assay repo.

